49615	Q0	exploredata-ZA8797_Varcaseid	4	4.4040647	instruments_tools	ISSP 1989 ZA1840 v2 ISSP 1997 ZA3090 v2 ISSP 2005 ZA4350 v3 ISSP 2015 ZA6770 CASEID Respondent Identification Numbers taken from the integrated data files unmodified ISSP 1989 This number uniquely identifies each repondent. The first two digits are identical with the country code the next five digits contain the original identification number.ISSP 2005 This number uniquely identifies each respondent. It is composed of two sections containing eight numbers in total. The first two digits are identical with the country codes 01 43 of variable COUNTRY . The digits following behind contain the original identification number.ISSP 2015 This variable holds a unique identification number to each respondent including the ISSP module year first 4 digits 2015 the ISO 3166 country code next 5 digits for countries without subsamples starting with 00 plus the three digits for the country code for countries with subsamples starting directly with the three digits country code supplemented by an appendix two digits long and the original identification number of the respondents the last 7 digits making an identification number of 16 numbers in total.
49615	Q0	exploredata-ZA8792_Varcaseid	5	4.3739467	instruments_tools	ISSP 1991 ZA2150 V2 ISSP 1998 ZA3190 V2 ISSP 2008 ZA4950 ZA5690 V3 ISSP 2018 ZA7570 ZA7630 CASEID Respondent Identification Numbers taken from the integrated data files unmodified in ISSP 1991 ISSP 1998 6 up to 7 digit ID number. The first first and second digit identifies the country the next five digits contain the original identification number. The ID number uniquely identifies each respondent within the respective dataset.in ISSP 2008 1 up to 8 digit numbers contain original identification of respondents without country identification. To provide a unique identification across the full integrated file it is necessary to combine V3 and V4 in ZA4950 .in ISSP 2018 This variable holds a unique identification number for each respondent including the ISSP module year first 4 digits 2018 the ISO 3166 country code next 5 digits for countries without subsamples starting with 00 plus the three digits for the country code for countries with subsamples starting directly with the three digits country code supplemented by an appendix two digits long and the original identification number of the respondents the last 7 digits making an identification number of 16 digits in total.
